      "hints": [
        "Set $f'(x) = x^2 - 6x + 8 \\ge 0 \\implies (x - 2)(x - 4) \\ge 0$.",
        "Identify that for $f$ to be increasing for all $x > n$, we must have $n \\ge 4$, so least integer $n = 4$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "An increasing function requires $f'(x) \\ge 0$ across its entire domain $x > n$:\n$$f'(x) = x^2 - 6x + 8 \\ge 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic derivative:\n$$(x - 2)(x - 4) \\ge 0$$",
        "Determine the intervals where $f'(x) \\ge 0$:\n$$x \\le 2 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x \\ge 4$$",
        "For the function to be increasing on the single uninterrupted domain $x > n$, the interval must lie entirely within $x \\ge 4$:\n$$n \\ge 4 \\implies \\text{Least possible integer value: } n = 4$$"
      ],
